| 10.2 | Call `RunnerProposals` from the absorb, on the proposing node, after the schema gate (M4) | Proposals are validated and silently dropped, so D15 is vacuous and the shipped CHANGELOG line is false | `runner_absorb_test#test_absorb_accepts_a_proposed_node` |
| 10.3 | Surface a refused proposal in the step report (M4) | A refusal is silent and the executor proposes the same thing every attempt | `runner_absorb_test#test_refused_proposal_is_reported` |
| 10.4 | Call `NodeWorktree.reap` once per step, after the reclaim pass (M5) | D26's reaper never runs and abandoned node worktrees accumulate forever | `runner_cli_test#test_step_reaps_stale_node_worktrees` |
| 10.5 | Release a node worktree on `superseded` and `abandoned` (M5) | `RunnerAnswer.respin` and `RunnerRewind` leave worktrees on disk, against D7 | `runner_absorb_test#test_superseded_node_releases_its_worktree` |
| 10.6 | Roll back a provisioned worktree when the packet build fails (M6) | A packet that cannot be built leaves an orphan worktree and the node is retried into the same orphan on every later step | `runner_dispatch_test#test_failed_packet_build_rolls_back_the_worktree` |
